          "The stated differentiation steps formally give p_tt + K ∂t(∂x u) = 0 and ∂x(∂t u) + (1/ρ)p_xx = 0; these displayed intermediate formulas are analyst expansions of the source's instructions [printed page 3, paragraph after (1.7); printed page 2, equation (1.5)].",
          "Commuting the mixed derivatives and eliminating them gives p_tt = (K/ρ)p_xx; identifying K/ρ with c² yields the displayed result in the intended real sound-speed setting [printed page 3, mixed-derivative elimination explanation and (1.7); printed page 2, c = √(K/ρ)]."
        ]
      },
      {
        "topic": "Scope and object roles",
